If you only needed MR or drain resistance to face him then it would be
worthwhile to switch out a weapon that provides MR (which is rare in
Spork) in favor of a weapon that grants drain resistance.

Since you need both then there's no reason to give up MR and drain
resistance can be gotten without using a weapon slot by becoming non-
human for a while.  (This route will not provide both MR and armor
protection at the same time.)

In either case you'll want multiple bless-damage-bonuses per round if
you don't feed him to a worm.

If your alignment is not C then you'll have drain resistance options
other than stormy and you can carry magic resistance without using a
weapon or armor slot.

By reducing Rogues to a single weapon skill, you'll be able to max out
spellcasting with slots to spare.

And yes the Nazies are now fifth on my geno list, after the flayers
and the two top Ls.

